  "notes": "Experimental diagnostic provider. Rows routed to each expert execute together through pinned oneDNN 3.12 BF16 gate, up, and down projections, preserving publisher row grouping and BF16 stage/weighted accumulation. A pinned three-token Ryzen generated replay is exact through layer 2, but full-model logits still diverge. Exactness remains artifact-, shape-, ISA-, and thread-specific. Requires caller-owned 64-byte aligned workspace and unique selected expert IDs per row. The generated-call wrapper hard-fails on invalid routing or workspace; direct native callers can use the status-returning workspace function. R*(12*H+16*I+8)+8*I bounds CKE staging only; a 32K-row build reserves about 1.54 GB, and oneDNN allocations are additional.",
  "numerical_contract": "moe_expert_pytorch_onednn_3_12_grouped_rows_bf16_stages_fp32_route_bf16_accum",
